{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) required for a string to return to its original form.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0  # Or handle as per requirements for empty string; 0 rotations means same string.\n    \n    # If the string consists of all identical characters (e.g., \"aaaa\"),\n    # one rotation will return the string to its original form.\n    # This also covers cases like \"a\" where one rotation brings it back.\n    if len(set(input_string)) == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    original_string = input_string\n    current_string = input_string\n    rotation_count = 0\n\n    while True:\n        # Perform one rotation: move the first character to the end\n        current_string = current_string[1:] + current_string[0]\n        rotation_count += 1\n\n        # Check if the rotated string matches the original\n        if current_string == original_string:\n            return rotation_count"}
