{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "from typing import Union\ndef recursive_list_sum(input_list: list) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively flattens a nested list and sums all its numerical elements.\n    Elements that are neither lists nor numbers are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for element in input_list:\n        if isinstance(element, list):\n            total += recursive_list_sum(element)\n        elif isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            total += element\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def max_difference(data: list[tuple[float | int, float | int]]) -> float | int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between pairs in a list of tuples.\n    Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n\n    differences = []\n    for pair in data:\n        diff = abs(pair[0] - pair[1])\n        differences.append(diff)\n\n    return max(differences)"}
