{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def _kadane_variant(transformed_array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies a Kadane's-like algorithm to find the maximum sum of a non-empty subarray.\n    This corresponds to the max difference between 0s (1) and 1s (-1).\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = transformed_array[0]\n    current_max = transformed_array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(transformed_array)):\n        current_max = max(transformed_array[i], current_max + transformed_array[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n    \n    return max_so_far\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring of the given binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge case: empty string as specified in the interface.\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    # Validate characters in the string, raising ValueError for non-binary chars.\n    _validate_binary_string(binary_string)\n\n    # Handle single character strings as specified in the interface.\n    if len(binary_string) == 1:\n        if binary_string == \"0\":\n            return 1\n        elif binary_string == \"1\":\n            return -1\n\n    # Transform the binary string: '0' becomes 1, '1' becomes -1.\n    transformed_array = [1 if char == '0' else -1 for char in binary_string]\n\n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm variant to find the maximum subarray sum.\n    return _kadane_variant(transformed_array)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def _get_divisors(number: int) -> set[int]:\n    \"\"\"Identifies all positive divisors for a given positive integer.\n    Returns a set of divisors.\"\"\"\n    divs = set()\n    for i in range(1, int(number**0.5) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            divs.add(i)\n            divs.add(number // i)\n    return divs\n\ndef _find_common_divisors(divisors1: set[int], divisors2: set[int]) -> set[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds common divisors between two sets of divisors.\n    Returns a set of common divisors.\"\"\"\n    return divisors1.intersection(divisors2)\n\ndef _sum_list_elements(numbers: set[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers in a set.\"\"\"\n    return sum(numbers)\n\ndef sum_common_divisors(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common divisors for two given numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisors1 = _get_divisors(num1)\n    divisors2 = _get_divisors(num2)\n    common_divs = _find_common_divisors(divisors1, divisors2)\n    return _sum_list_elements(common_divs)"}
