{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(numbers: list, start_index: int, end_index: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates the input list and indices. Raises ValueError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(start_index, int) or not isinstance(end_index, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Start and end indices must be integers.\")\n\n    # If start_index is greater than end_index, it represents an empty range, which is valid and sums to 0.\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        return\n\n    # For non-empty ranges (start_index <= end_index), validate list content and indices.\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        # If the list is empty and start_index <= end_index, it's an invalid attempt to sum a non-empty range.\n        raise ValueError(\"Cannot sum from an empty list with a specified non-empty range.\")\n\n    if not (0 <= start_index < list_length):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Start index {start_index} is out of bounds for list of length {list_length}.\")\n    if not (0 <= end_index < list_length):\n        raise ValueError(f\"End index {end_index} is out of bounds for list of length {list_length}.\")\n\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        if not isinstance(numbers[i], (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a number. Found: {type(numbers[i]).__name__}.\")\ndef sum_range_list(numbers: list, start_index: int, end_index: int) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range (inclusive).\"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(numbers, start_index, end_index)\n\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        return 0\n\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        total += numbers[i]\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "def check_type(input_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in the input_tuple have the same data type.\n    Returns True for an empty tuple, or if all elements are of the same type.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_tuple:\n        return True\n\n    first_element_type = type(input_tuple[0])\n    for element in input_tuple[1:]:\n        if type(element) is not first_element_type:\n            return False\n    return True"}
