{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_index = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_index\ndef _find_last_occurrence(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    last_index = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_index = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_index\ndef is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_index = _find_first_occurrence(array, n, element)\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_index = _find_last_occurrence(array, n, element)\n    occurrence_count = last_index - first_index + 1\n    majority_threshold = n / 2.0\n\n    return occurrence_count > majority_threshold"}
