{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence from the input array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    if len(arr) == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    dp_inc = list(arr)\n    dp_dec = list(arr)\n\n    # Calculate increasing subsequence sums ending at each index\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dp_inc[i] = max(dp_inc[i], dp_inc[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate decreasing subsequence sums starting at each index\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dp_dec[i] = max(dp_dec[i], dp_dec[j] + arr[i])\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    # Combine increasing and decreasing parts to find the maximum bitonic sum\n    # Subtract arr[i] to avoid double counting the peak element\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = dp_inc[i] + dp_dec[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\n    It iteratively increments an integer `i` until `i*i` exceeds the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find the smallest integer `i` such that `i*i` is greater than `number`.\n    # Start checking from `i = 0`.\n    i = 0\n    while i * i <= number:\n        i += 1\n    return i * i"}
