{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(input_array: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum contiguous sub-array sum in the array conceptually repeated k times.\n    Utilizes Kadane's algorithm and handles various scenarios based on k and the array's total sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _kadane(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Implements Kadane's algorithm to find the largest sum of a contiguous sub-array.\"\"\"\n        if not arr:\n            return 0\n        max_so_far = float('-inf')\n        current_max = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            current_max += x\n            if current_max > max_so_far:\n                max_so_far = current_max\n            if current_max < 0:\n                current_max = 0\n        return max_so_far if max_so_far != float('-inf') else max(arr) # Handles all negative numbers case\n\n    if not input_array:\n        return 0\n    if k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    kadane_single = _kadane(input_array)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane_single\n\n    total_sum = sum(input_array)\n\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    max_prefix_sum = float('-inf')\n    for x in input_array:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    max_suffix_sum = float('-inf')\n    for x in reversed(input_array):\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    if total_sum <= 0:\n        # If the total sum is non-positive, repeating the array multiple times won't improve a sum\n        # that spans across the array more than twice. We only need to check one or two repetitions.\n        kadane_double = _kadane(input_array + input_array)\n        return max(kadane_single, kadane_double)\n    else:\n        # If total_sum is positive, an optimal solution might include (k-2) full repetitions\n        # of the array plus a prefix and a suffix.\n        kadane_multiple = max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum\n        return max(kadane_single, kadane_multiple)"}
