{"task_id": "Mbpp/404", "solution": "from typing import Union\ndef minimum(num1: Union[int, float], num2: Union[int, float]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines and returns the smaller of two numerical inputs.\n\n    Args:\n        num1 (Union[int, float]): The first numerical input.\n        num2 (Union[int, float]): The second numerical input.\n\n    Returns:\n        Union[int, float]: The smaller of the two input numbers.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> minimum(1, 2)\n        1\n        >>> minimum(5, 5)\n        5\n        >>> minimum(10, -2)\n        -2\n        >>> minimum(3.14, 2.71)\n        2.71\n    \"\"\"\n    if num1 <= num2:\n        return num1\n    else:\n        return num2"}
