{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    This handles positive, negative, and zero elements correctly.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize current_max and current_min to the first element.\n    # These track the maximum and minimum product ending at the current position.\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n    overall_max_product = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        current_num = arr[i]\n\n        # Store previous max_so_far before it's updated.\n        # This is needed because current_min might use the old max_so_far.\n        temp_max = max_so_far\n\n        # Update max_so_far: current_num itself, current_num * previous max, current_num * previous min.\n        # The product with previous min is important if current_num is negative.\n        max_so_far = max(current_num, current_num * temp_max, current_num * min_so_far)\n\n        # Update min_so_far: current_num itself, current_num * previous max, current_num * previous min.\n        # The product with previous max is important if current_num is negative.\n        min_so_far = min(current_num, current_num * temp_max, current_num * min_so_far)\n\n        # Update overall_max_product with the maximum product found so far.\n        overall_max_product = max(overall_max_product, max_so_far)\n\n    return overall_max_product"}
