{"task_id": "Mbpp/476", "solution": "def big_sum(arr: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest and smallest value in a given array.\n    Raises TypeError or ValueError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not arr:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array cannot be empty.\")\n\n    # Validate elements are numeric\n    for x in arr:\n        if not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the array must be numeric.\")\n\n    min_val = arr[0]\n    max_val = arr[0]\n\n    for num in arr:\n        if num < min_val:\n            min_val = num\n        if num > max_val:\n            max_val = num\n            \n    return float(min_val + max_val)"}
