{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of the input list where every pair is mutually divisible.\n    Uses dynamic programming after sorting the numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Sort the input list to enable dynamic programming\n    numbers.sort()\n\n    # dp[i] will store the size of the largest divisible subset ending with numbers[i]\n    dp = [1] * n\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in i_range(0, i):\n            # Check if numbers[i] is divisible by numbers[j]\n            # Since the list is sorted, numbers[j] <= numbers[i]\n            if numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\n    return max(dp)"}
