{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\nNumber = Union[int, float]\ndef get_median(list1: List[Number], list2: List[Number], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    This function finds the N-th and (N+1)-th elements of the conceptually merged\n    sorted list (1-based indexing) and returns their average in O(N) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    count = 0\n    m1 = -1.0\n    m2 = -1.0\n\n    while count <= n:\n        if i == n:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = float(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = float(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] < list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = float(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = float(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n        count += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
