{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates (including itself) for a given coordinate tuple.\n\n    Args:\n        coordinate_tuple: A tuple (x, y) representing the center coordinate.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):\n            adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    return adjacent_coords"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Returns radius squared for non-negative radii, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    else:\n        # The largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle has its base as the diameter\n        # and its apex at any point on the arc. Its height will be the radius.\n        # Area = 0.5 * base * height = 0.5 * (2 * radius) * radius = radius * radius.\n        return radius * radius"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Moves all zero elements to the end of the input_list, preserving the relative order\n    of non-zero elements, and returns the modified list.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_zero_elements = []\n    zero_count = 0\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_elements.append(element)\n\n    input_list.clear()\n    input_list.extend(non_zero_elements)\n    input_list.extend([0] * zero_count)\n\n    return input_list"}
