{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list by a specified number of items to the right direction.\n    Handles empty lists and rotation counts larger than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(input_list)\n    effective_rotation_count = rotation_count % n\n\n    # The new list is formed by taking the last 'effective_rotation_count' elements\n    # and concatenating them with the first 'n - effective_rotation_count' elements.\n    rotated_list = input_list[n - effective_rotation_count:] + input_list[:n - effective_rotation_count]\n    \n    return rotated_list"}
